From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:09:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] usb: typec: mux: wcd939x-usbss: Fix the MG2_MISC register
 address

The probe enables the 2x dynamic boost of the MG1 and MG2 OVP
comparators by setting bit 5 of their MISC registers. MG1_MISC is
correct at 0x27, but MG2_MISC is defined as 0x30.

In Qualcomm's register map of the WCD939x USB subsystem
(wcd-usbss-registers.h in the vendor kernel) the OVP block starts at
0x1f and each MG switch has four registers: EN, BIAS, CTSNS_CTL and
MISC. MG1 uses 0x24-0x27, so MG1_MISC is 0x27, and MG2 uses
0x28-0x2b, so MG2_MISC is 0x2b; this driver already uses 0x28 and 0x29
for MG2_EN and MG2_BIAS. 0x30 is TOP_MISC2, outside the OVP switch
registers.

So the probe never enabled the dynamic boost of the MG2 OVP and set
bit 5 of TOP_MISC2 instead. Use 0x2b.

Found by Reixo while porting the WCD9395 to the RedMagic 11 Pro
(Reixo0/nx809j-mainline); the address is re-derived here from the
vendor register map.

Fixes: 36d586c0570e ("usb: typec: mux: add Qualcomm WCD939X USB SubSystem Altmode Mux driver")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
index 53bcd9eddb81..322c185a54dc 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
 
 #define WCD_USBSS_MG2_BIAS_PCOMP_DYN_BST_EN				BIT(3)
 
-#define WCD_USBSS_MG2_MISC			0x30
+#define WCD_USBSS_MG2_MISC			0x2b
 
 #define WCD_USBSS_MG2_MISC_PCOMP_2X_DYN_BST_ON_EN			BIT(5)
 
